cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use OpenCarMind or the CarMind models in research, please cite this repository.
title: "OpenCarMind: an open-source OBD2 logger for the ESP32 with TinyML on the board"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rahman
    given-names: Alvee
version: 2.5.1
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/AlveeeRahman/OpenCarMind
url: https://alveeerahman.github.io/OpenCarMind/
keywords:
  - OBD-II
  - ESP32-S3
  - TinyML
  - on-device learning
  - automotive data logging
abstract: >-
  Firmware, desktop app and model card for an ESP32-S3 car data logger that runs a quantised
  convolutional network on the chip. The CarMind R.E.V model keeps learning the car it rides in,
  with an outlier-robust recursive least-squares read-out for fuel rate and a learned airflow
  constant that sizes a physics torque estimate.
